    "turn_text": "genius. And guess what? It's totally free. So go on, download the Experian app. Trust me, having a BFF like this is a total game changer. So you've taken this pledge. So you're not spending 75%, 50%. I mean, can you talk about how much of your time you think you spend asking for? I actually have never been in any of these rooms where you are making phone calls. Wow. Hopefully that answers your question. Wow. So to me, even though I'm a member of Congress, it's still a myth that these rooms exist. Wow. Well, good for you. That's amazing. That's amazing. On January 6th, you talked about this a little bit, you feared for your life. What was that day like for you? Yeah, I think the part that I haven't talked a lot about is that for the four months leading up to January 6th, because the president and all of his rallies would mention my name, I had, you know, active assassination plots and death threats. And so I had to have a full capital police detail, which is six cars. three cars, six officers in plane clothes that are with you every day in an armored car that you travel in. And when the day came for us to be here, they were like, we will take you right before debate begins. My pickup time was 1 p.m. We arrived here. Again, it was COVID. You know, majority of my staff was in here. There was just one person on the staff assigned to help me navigate the day. And then my husband was like, I'm too scared for you to go almost all come and came with me. And I remember, you know, like I have to find tennis shoes to wear today, right? Because I was like, we might be running around. And when we got in the car to come here, I could hear on their radio, because it was a police car, that there were pipe bombs that were being found, that there was a building that was being evacuated, one of the buildings that houses members of Congress offices. And we came into the office maybe 10 minutes after that.",
